Q: Unit Testing Roslyn Diagnostic with External Project Reference A: <p>So this turned out to be easier than originally expected.  I was able to use the <code>SourceText.From</code> method which worked as expected:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>    [Fact]
    [Trait(&quot;Area&quot;, &quot;Roslyn&quot;)]
    [Trait(&quot;Type&quot;, &quot;Analyzer&quot;)]
    public async Task ValidateAs_InvalidAlias()
    {
        var source = SourceText.From(&quot;&quot;&quot;
                                #nullable enable

                                using System;
                                using Company.Validator.Shared.Attributes;
                                using Company.Validator.Shared.Enums;
                                using Company.Validator.Shared.Models;

                                public partial class Program
                                {
                                    [ValidateAs(&quot;1Alias&quot;, StringOptions.AllowNull)]
                                    public string? ValidateAsProperty { get; set; }

                                    public static void Main()
                                    {
                                        Console.WriteLine(&quot;Hello, World!&quot;);
                                        Console.ReadKey();
                                    }
                                }
                                &quot;&quot;&quot;);

        var expected = new[] { CompanyValidatorAnalyzer.DD_INVALID_ALIAS };
        var actual =
            await source.GetDiagnostics&lt;CompanyValidatorAnalyzer&gt;([typeof(Shared.Attributes.ValidateAsAttribute)]);

        DiagnosticResultsHelper.VerifyDiagnostic(expected, actual).Should().BeTrue();
    }
</code></pre>

Q: Select without a FROM clause in Oracle A: <p>Starting from version 23 it is possible to omit <code>FROM</code> clause.</p>
<hr />
<p>Side note: <code>FROM DUAL</code> is present in the query:</p>
<pre><code>SELECT 42 AS result;
</code></pre>
<p>After expanding it:</p>
<pre><code>declare
  x VARCHAR2(1000);
begin
 dbms_utility.expand_sql_text(
        input_sql_text =&gt; 'SELECT 42 AS result',
        output_sql_text =&gt; x);
  dbms_output.put_line(x);
end;
/
</code></pre>
<pre><code>SELECT 42 &quot;RESULT&quot; FROM &quot;SYS&quot;.&quot;DUAL&quot; &quot;A1&quot;
</code></pre>

Q: Fade out on image hover not working (css) A: <p>Your selectors are wrong, see: <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Selectors/Selectors_and_combinators" rel="nofollow noreferrer">mdn selectors</a> Since you are already using classes, your css definitions can use those. Instead of building a kind of path to the element <code>body main .proyectos div</code>, <code>.proyectos &gt; div</code> with the child selector <code>&gt;</code> works. But the div also has a class, which makes it even easier to select with <code>.galería_landing</code> :</p>
<pre><code>.galería_landing {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(11, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: repeat(2, 50%);
  grid-gap: 2%;
  margin-bottom: 10%;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Selecting the children which should apply the :hover effect can utilyze the child selector:</p>
<pre><code>.galería_landing &gt; article {
  transition: opacity .3s ease-in-out;
  -moz-transition: opacity .3s ease-in-out;
  -webkit-transition: opacity .3s ease-in-out;
}

.galería_landing &gt; article:hover{
  opacity: 0.9;
}
</code></pre>
<p>It's important to define the trasition in the base element without the hovered state, otherwise it will be removed when the hover ends and no transitioning back would be applied.</p>
